/*
:name: state_window_delay
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: state_window_delay
:pyrope_top: state_window_delay
:equiv_lec_grep: (?m)^lec: '[^']+' PROVEN equivalent
:equiv_lec_grep: state window\(s\): narrower flop paired with the live slice
*/
// A NARROWER flop against the live slice of a WIDER one (suggestions6 1.5).
//
// The golden (bedrock br_delay, Width=8, NumStages=4) keeps a packed
// `stages[4:0][7:0]` vector whose entry 0 is the input wire: its flop is 40
// bits wide, but bits 7:0 are never stored nor read. The Pyrope keeps only the
// four stored stages, so its register is 32 bits. pass/lec/query.cpp's state
// windows pair the 32-bit flop with bits 39:8 of the 40-bit one; without them
// the pair aligns at bit 0, induction never closes, and the run stops at a
// bounded PASS(6). The greps pin the UNBOUNDED proof and the mechanism.
pub mod state_window_delay(clk:Clock, `in`:U8, rst:U1) -> (out:U8@[], out_stages:U40@[]) {
  reg stages:U32:[reset_pin=rst] = 0
  stages = (stages#[0..<24] << 8) | `in`
  out = stages#[24..<32]
  out_stages = (stages << 8) | `in`
}
